    thinking: "**Analyzing the Project Brief**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s request and requirements, getting a solid grip on the task at hand. Specifically, I\'m focusing on building \"RuangRAB \342\200\224 AI Quantity Takeoff & Kalkulator Volume Konstruksi.\" I\'ve got the master prompt in Indonesian and a design mockup image to work with.\n\n\n**Defining the Dashboard Structure**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the dashboard\'s layout, ensuring it mirrors the provided image and project brief. I\'m focusing on the left sidebar, header with project info, four-step stepper, document and manual input cards, filterable tables, and the right panel with AI assistant, project summary, and Excel export button, and the bottom recap. I\'m taking notes from the example layout.\n\n\n**Implementing Core Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core features. This includes real Excel exports using `exceljs`, robust project management with localStorage/IndexedDB, and a flexible hybrid floor system with basement, multiple floors, and roof options. I\'m also mapping a built-in catalog from USC JSON with traceable references and formulas. The AI Assistant using the Gemini API will handle drawing and document analysis, using a secure backend route. Lastly, I\'m focusing on visual fidelity to match the mockup.\n\n\n"
