  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Workbook Structure**\n\nI\'ve established a clear structural breakdown for the workbook. The initial section, \"Volume Persiapan Dll,\" will encompass preparatory works: site clearing (using length and width), temporary fencing, bouwplank, and tool storage. Subsequent sections will address electrical works, specifying point lights, power outlets, and single switches.\n\n\n**Expanding Structural Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now delving into the structural volumes. This involves defining the scope of work for sanitation tasks like faucets, septic tanks, and relevant piping. Also, I\'m analyzing the \"Volume Struktural\" segment, which includes detailed items such as earthworks and backfilling, the specifics of foundation types with associated concrete grades and reinforcement details, and various concrete elements like pedestals, sloofs, and columns.\n\n\n**Detailing Structural Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing specific structural components. I\'ve broken down Kolom Type K2 (30x30), including Beton, Tulangan Pokok, Begel, and Bekisting, and I\'m also specifying Kolom Praktis by its total length. Balok Type 1 and Type 2 are next, each with Beton, Tulangan Pokok, Begel, and Bekisting. Kantilever beams, latei, and bordes are also being itemized. I\'m additionally accounting for Anak Tangga and various Plat Lantai elements across different elevation levels. Finally, I\'ve outlined the work needed for the roof, including its framework and covering.\n\n\n**Enumerating Architectural Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the architectural aspects. I\'ve begun itemizing components within the \"Volume Arsitektural\" section. Specifically, I\'m focusing on \"Pekerjaan Pasangan Dinding dan Plesteran,\" which includes calculating materials for lightweight brick installation, plastering, and acian. Also, the specification covers wall tiles for the toilets and other finishes. I\'m moving on to outlining flooring elements, including the specification of the finishing. I\'m also cataloging the items associated with Painting and ceilings.\n\n\n**Cataloging Architectural Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing doors, windows, and related architectural elements. I\'ve specified metal hollow framework (35x35) and gypsum moldings (10cm). I\'m itemizing various door types (P1-P4), noting their aluminum frames (4\"/5x10), panel doors, clear glass (5mm), handles, hinges, mortise locks, and bolts. For windows (types 1-4), I\'m cataloging aluminum frames, window panels, glass, latches/bolts, swing hinges, and locks, along with bouvenlights with aluminum frames and frosted/clear glass.\n\n\n**Outlining Project Interface**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the user interface. I\'ve broken down the workflow into four steps: data entry, image input, volume calculation, and report generation. The interface will feature two primary action cards: one for uploading plans (image or PDF) with a drag-and-drop area and another for manual data entry, each with a clear call to action. I\'ve designed the work table section with filter tabs, a search bar, a \"Add Job\" button, and an accordion for floor-based organization, each with the required columns for data presentation and action. A right sidebar is planned to host other features.\n\n\n**Designing Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific interface components. I\'ve conceived of two primary widgets: an optional AI assistant beta that helps read images and documents to suggest parameters and a \"Project Summary\" card with project name, floor count, item count, status, and an export button. I\'m also building recap cards for volume, area, length, and item counts, and a left navigation sidebar with links to various sections. A bottom tip card provides a reminder about parameter accuracy.\n\n\n"
