  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Server Setup**\n\nI\'m exploring the `createServer` function in `vite` and thinking about running a development server with `tsx server.ts`. I\'m also considering Vite\'s proxy and `vite.middlewares` options for backend routing, keeping in mind the guideline on full-stack applications. I want to determine the best approach.\n\n\n**Defining Application Architecture**\n\nI\'ve decided to structure the application around a `server.ts` entry point using Express, with `vite.middlewares` for the development environment. I\'ll configure a full-stack start command in `package.json` with `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`. I\'ve confirmed that changing the dev script to `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` will correctly launch the server on port 3000. I\'m now focusing on architecting the core components. I am using semantic catalogs mapped from USC JSON data in `src/data/catalog.ts`.\n\n\n**Calculating Material Needs**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on calculating material requirements for the project. I\'m focusing on the \"Volume Persiapan Dll\" and \"Volume Struktural\" sheets, specifically, calculating volumes for the building\'s base. For the first sheet, I\'m calculating areas for gudang material and gudang alat using their formulas. For the second sheet, I am calculating volumes for excavations using specific formulas for stone foundations and footplates, and I am ensuring units are correct.\n\n\n**Analyzing Volume Calculations**\n\nI\'m now diving into detailed volume calculations, focusing on formulas for various elements. I\'m calculating the fill material for floor elevation and under footings, ensuring units are correct. I\'ve also formulated calculations for stone foundations and footplates, considering trapezoidal and cubic sections. Now, I\'m working through Beton K-350 for footplates, including reinforcement and formwork, and the concrete work for pedestal columns. I\'m meticulously cross-referencing formulas and units.\n\n\n**Detailing Construction Elements**\n\nI\'m now cataloging construction elements and their associated calculations. I\'ve broken down rebar configurations for 16D19 Ulir, \303\23010-150 stirrups, and formwork. Next, I am itemizing components for pedestal columns, including concrete, reinforcement, and formwork. I\'ve got a plan for sloof calculations, covering both main and support reinforcement. I\'m also preparing to specify calculations for K1 and K2 columns, as well as practical columns. I\'m meticulously itemizing materials for Type 1 and Type 2 beams, ensuring all aspects are covered. Finally, I will determine the Kantilever Balok requirements.\n\n\n**Enumerating Component Volumes**\n\nI\'m now detailing calculations for beams and stair components. This includes the Balok Latei 15x25 with its specific reinforcement and formwork, and the Balok Bordes Tangga with corresponding details. I have also formulated Anak Tangga, Plat Bordes Tangga, and Plat Lantai P1, focusing on Beton, reinforcement, and Bekisting, covering each with accurate formulas.\n\n\n**Calculating Architectural Volumes**\n\nI\'m now detailing architectural material quantities, starting with calculating areas. I\'m focusing on \"Gajah Mini\" and \"Batu Koral\" in square meters. Then, I am moving to Sheet 3, the \"Volume Arsitektural,\" and itemizing materials like Lightweight Brick, Plaster, and Ceramic Wall Tiles, utilizing formulas for calculations. I\'m meticulously detailing each element, including units and specific spreadsheet cell references.\n\n\n\n**Enumerating Finishing Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing architectural finishing materials and volumes. I am itemizing and quantifying each element, including wood-motif tiles, concrete floor finishing, and various painting types. I\'m noting specific cells for all of the calculations. I\'ve broken down requirements for gypsum, listing, and various door and window types. This includes specifying aluminium frames, glass areas, and hardware, and have detailed components for all types. I\'m focusing on creating deterministic calculations.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing a calculation engine in `src/services/calculationEngine.ts`. This involves a focus on safe formula parsing and evaluation, ensuring no use of `eval`. I\'m also preparing the engine to handle multi-component items like beams and walls with segments and for real-time recalculation based on updated parameters.\n\n\n**Developing Calculation Engine**\n\nNow I\'m making progress on the calculation engine\'s features. Specifically, I\'m integrating numerical precision and Indonesian formatting (commas and dots). I\'m also ensuring the engine handles various cases, including empty values, division by zero, and dependency checks. I\'ve defined status indicators for calculation states. I\'m also planning the storage of project data within local storage.\n\n\n**Designing Project Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on the user interface, aiming for an intuitive workflow. I\'m prioritizing key elements like a header with project information and controls, a clear 4-step stepper bar, and two distinct card options for data input (uploading images or entering manual data). I plan to use a filterable table to display calculated results, complete with actionable components.\n\n\n**Designing AI Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now detailing an AI-assisted data integration workflow. This includes an \"AI Assistant Panel\" with drawing uploads that sends data to `/api/gemini/extract-dimensions`, generating a draft table for user review. I\'m prioritizing human-in-the-loop validation, offering \'Setujui\', \'Edit\', or \'Tolak\' actions before moving data to the calculator. I\'m planning a summary view with key volume totals and an Excel export with detailed calculation sheets, using `exceljs`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2136079"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * RuangRAB - Type Definitions\\n * Quantity Takeoff & Konstruksi Volume Calculator\\n */\\n\\nexport type WorkCategory = \'Persiapan Dll\' | \'Struktural\' | \'Arsitektural\' | \'MEP\';\\n\\nexport type CalculationStatus =\\n  | \'Lengkap\'\\n  | \'Perlu Input\'\\n  | \'Perlu Verifikasi\'\\n  | \'Rumus Belum Dipetakan\'\\n  | \'Kesalahan Perhitungan\'\\n  | \'Tidak Digunakan\';\\n\\nexport type ParameterType = \'number\' | \'text\' | \'select\';\\n\\nexport interface ParameterItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  label: string;\\n  value: number | string | null;\\n  unit: string;\\n  type?: ParameterType;\\n  required?: boolean;\\n  source?: \'manual\' | \'ai\' | \'derived\' | \'reference\';\\n  notes?: string;\\n  excelCellRef?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface WorkComponent {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string; // e.g., \\\"Bagian 1\\\", \\\"Balok B1\\\", \\\"Dinding Depan\\\"\\n  parameters: Record<string, number | null>;\\n  formulaText?: string;\\n  computedVolume?: number | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CatalogWorkItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  code?: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  category: WorkCategory;\\n  subCategory?: string;\\n  floorRule: \'umum\' | \'per_lantai\' | \'atap_saja\' | \'fondasi_saja\';\\n  description: string;\\n  defaultUnit: string;\\n  formulaDisplay: string;\\n  excelSheet: string;\\n  excelCell: string;\\n  excelFormula?: string;\\n  parameters: ParameterItem[];\\n  defaultComponents?: WorkComponent[];\\n  calculationMethod: (params: Record<string, number>, components?: WorkComponent[]) => number | null;\\n  verificationStatus: CalculationStatus;\\n  verificationNotes?: string;\\n  hasExternalRef?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ProjectWorkItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  catalogId?: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  category: WorkCategory;\\n  subCategory?: string;\\n  floorId: string; // \\\"umum\\\" or floorId\\n  unit: string;\\n  formulaDisplay: string;\\n  parameters: ParameterItem[]