  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Request**\n\nI\'m diving into the user\'s detailed report regarding RuangRAB. Currently, I\'m meticulously breaking down the bug report and enhancement specification. This includes addressing the \"Error 503\" and the \"model experiencing high demand.\" I\'m carefully sifting through the details to map out a clear action plan.\n\n\n**Implementing Retry Logic**\n\nI\'m focused on implementing robust retry mechanisms. I\'m building in exponential backoff with jitter and a maximum of three attempts, making sure to respect `Retry-After`. I\'m also meticulously crafting the logic to avoid retrying for client-side errors (4xx codes). A fallback system is crucial, so I\'m integrating secondary models like `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` or `gemini-flash-latest` if the primary model fails. I\'m also planning to prevent accidental duplicate requests. If the whole retry process fails I will clear the Indonesian message with a \"Coba Lagi\" button.\n\n\n**Devising Backup Data Generation**\n\nI\'m now integrating a backup data generation strategy. If all else fails, I\'ll generate fake AI data to ensure a response. Next, I\'m working to implement the units and scale settings before the analysis.\nI\'ll also implement a dropdown for the project\'s floors and prioritize reading dimensions directly from the uploaded images. I\'m also adding multiple file types like PDF, JPG, and PNG as acceptable uploads. I\'m building \"Mulai Analisis AI\" button.\n\n\n**Calculating Unit Conversions**\n\nI\'m now establishing unit conversion calculations to translate real-world sizes accurately. I\'m focusing on storing original values and units alongside converted metrics in meters. I will be calculating these based on the user\'s unit selection, updating the displayed unit in the UI after the read for maximum flexibility.\n\n\n**Extracting Dimensional Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on the specific dimensional data provided, meticulously interpreting the room dimensions and stair details. I\'m prioritizing accurate extraction of building dimensions, room names, and wall lengths from this input. The goal is to accurately represent these real dimensions within the model for analysis. I\'m working to integrate a way to accurately read FFL measurements.\n\n\n**Refining UI Text**\n\nI\'m now revising the text in `AddWorkModal.tsx` based on the user\'s screenshot. The subtitle will become \"Pilih pekerjaan dari katalog atau tambahkan pekerjaan baru.\" The tabs are now \"Katalog Pekerjaan (49)\" and \"Pekerjaan Baru,\" dynamically updating the catalog count. I will also be removing all visible Excel references. I\'m focusing on displaying more user-friendly elements in the cards.\n\n\n"
