  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Fetch Request**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the fetch request within `AIAssistantModal.tsx`, specifically line 191. I\'m examining how it\'s structured, its use of the `/api/gemini/extract-dimensions` endpoint, and the POST method with JSON content. This will help refine the prompt for dimension extraction. I\'m also considering the implications of the body data being passed to this endpoint.\n\n\n**Investigating the Response**\n\nI\'m now investigating a specific error: `Unexpected token \'<\', \"<!doctype \"... is not valid JSON`. The root cause seems to be HTML being returned instead of JSON. This occurs when the server returns an error page, like a 404, 500, or a payload-too-large error. The Vite dev server or Express\'s default error handler, or Cloud Run can trigger this response. I\'m checking situations such as a large base64 payload.\n\n\n**Addressing the Middleware Errors**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of `express.json` errors and how they manifest in the frontend. It looks like an unhandled error in the Express middleware results in an HTML error page being returned. I\'m focusing on the unconditional call to `response.json()` in the frontend, which doesn\'t check for JSON content type or HTTP status. This suggests a potential vulnerability to unexpected HTML responses. I\'m also reviewing the route order in `server.ts` and considering adding explicit error handling middleware in Express.\n\n\n"
