  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Upload Overlap**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the redundant image upload sections in Section A. The \"Upload Image/PDF\" card and the AI Assistant modal\'s upload feature seem to serve the same purpose, leading to user confusion. I\'m exploring the implications of this duplication to determine the best path forward.\n\n\n**Consolidating Upload Points**\n\nI\'ve decided to eliminate the separate \"Upload Image/PDF\" card. The plan is to fully integrate the AI Assistant \342\200\223 Auto Quantity Takeoff section into the primary area above the job list. I\'ll retain the file upload capabilities within the AI Assistant. This approach keeps the unit selection and analysis initiation, while merging functions. Manual input will remain as an alternative, located close to the Assistant. Finally, an AI results button will link the work to the calculator.\n\n\n**Refining UI Integration**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to the hero section approach. The AI Assistant, with its enhanced upload and configuration features, will take center stage above the work list. I\'ve confirmed the right-hand panel simplification; removing the redundant AI Assistant card is key. I\'m exploring an embedded Auto Quantity Takeoff experience that is integrated and interactive, with direct access to data settings.\n\n\n**Exploring Inline AI Results**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to present AI results. Should I offer quick, inline inspections, with an option to expand for a deeper look? Ideally, I\'d like to put a unified Auto Quantity Takeoff component directly on the page. The AI section should include file uploads, specific settings (units, scale, target floor), and a multi-step analysis button with progress indicators. Post-analysis, a summary banner should appear, with a direct link to view the generated drafts in the calculator. Manual input should also be accessible nearby. I\'m moving on to consider the sections F, G, H, I.\n\n\n**Implementing Floor-Based Additions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a more intuitive approach to adding work items. The plan is to place \"+ Tambah Pekerjaan\" buttons directly within each floor group (General & Foundation, Floor 1, Floor 2, etc.). Each button will automatically assign new work to its respective floor, simplifying the process. I\'ll make the floor group name visible in the \"Tambah Pekerjaan\" modal and ensure that the user can still manually adjust the floor assignment if necessary. I\'ll maintain safeguards to prevent unintentional floor modifications.\n\n\n**Defining Multi-Select Function**\n\nI\'m now outlining the \"Add Multiple Works\" feature, triggered by the \"+ Add Work\" button. The objective is a modal or catalog panel with job categories and a search function. I\'m focusing on checkbox-based multi-selection, and a \"Add X Works\" button. Selected works, by default, will be assigned to the open floor group.\n\n\n"
