  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Transform **RuangRAB** (AI Quantity Takeoff & Kalkulator Volume Konstruksi) from a single-user USC demo into a multi-user, public-ready AI Quantity Takeoff platform.\n   - **Key Requirements & Deliverables**:\n     1. **User Authentication & Accounts (Sign In & Create Account)**:\n        - Landing/Auth page before accessing the dashboard with **Sign In** and **Create Account / Sign Up** tabs, plus Google Sign-In (`signInWithPopup`) and secure Email/Password authentication.\n        - Sign Up fields: Full Name, Email, Password, Confirm Password, User Role/Type (`Student`, `Estimator`, `Other`).\n        - Features: Email/password validation, show/hide password toggle, forgot password flow, user-friendly Indonesian error messages, logout, and route/view protection.\n        - Remove hardcoded developer identity (\"Adjie / Estimator\" in `Header.tsx`). Display the logged-in user\'s name, email, role (`Student` / `Estimator` / `Other`), initials avatar, account settings modal, and logout button.\n        - Isolate user data so each user only accesses their own projects and documents (with automatic migration of any existing local projects into the user\'s account without data loss).\n     2. **Default Project Without USC Demo Data**:\n        - New users / new default projects must start as a clean template (`Proyek Baru`) with standard floor groups (`Umum & Pondasi`, `Lantai 1`, etc.) and empty/unfilled parameters\342\200\224**no hardcoded Gedung USC name or pre-filled USC dimensions/volumes**.\n        - Preserve existing saved projects if present in storage.\n        - Provide a **User Overview / Projects Hub** after login showing: welcome message with user\'s name, project count summary, last opened project, \"Buat Proyek Baru\" button, list of user\'s projects, and recent activity.\n     3. **Standardized Structural & Construction Catalog (`Katalog Pekerjaan`)**:\n        - Generalize catalog items so they are not tied to USC dimensions:\n          - Columns: `Kolom K1`, `Kolom K2`, `Kolom K3`, `Kolom Praktis`, `Kolom Kustom` (parameters: `lebar`, `tebal`/`panjang_sisi`, `tinggi`, `jumlah` \342\200\224 all default `value: null`, no hardcoded 50\303\22750 cm or 30\303\22730 cm defaults).\n          - Beams: `Balok B1`, `Balok B2`, `Balok B3`, `Balok Induk`, `Balok Anak`, `Balok Bordes`, `Ring Balok`, `Balok Kustom` (parameters: `panjang_total`, `lebar`, `tinggi` \342\200\224 all default `value: null`).\n          - Sloof: `Sloof S1`, `Sloof S2`, `Sloof S3`, `Sloof Kustom` (parameters: `panjang_total`, `lebar`, `tinggi` \342\200\224 all default `value: null`).\n          - Other elements: Pondasi, Plat Lantai, Plat Tangga, Tangga, Dinding, dll. with generic templates and `value: null` defaults while preserving verified mathematical formulas internally.\n     4. **Intuitive Vertical Parameter Input Form (`WorkDetailModal.tsx`)**:\n        - Replace cramped horizontal parameter inputs with a clear vertical/stacked layout where each parameter label is directly above its input field, with explicit units, informative placeholders, required (`*`) indicators, empty-parameter highlights, live numeric validation (never silently treating empty as `0`), mathematical formula display, and live volume calculation preview.\n     5. **Multi-Type Engineering Drawing AI Reader & Segment-Based Beam/Sloof Length Calculation**:\n        - Classify each page/region of uploaded PDFs/images into specific drawing types:\n          1. `Denah Arsitektur`, 2. `Denah Kolom`, 3. `Denah Balok`, 4. `Denah Sloof`, 5. `Denah Pondasi`, 6. `Potongan Bangunan`, 7. `Tampak Bangunan`, 8. `Detail Tangga`, 9. `Detail Pondasi`, 10. `Detail Sambungan`, 11. `Detail Penulangan`, 12. `Tabel Dimensi dan Penulangan`, 13. `Detail Konstruksi Lainnya`.\n        - Tag every extracted item with page number, drawing type, element name, element code (e.g., `S.1`, `B1`, `K1`), dimension, unit, grid/location (`As A-D`, `As 1-7`), source info, and confidence.\n        - Cross-reference information across drawing types/regions (e.g., matching `S.1` or `K1` on the plan with `S.1` `40 x 60` in the schedule/detail table on the same or another page) and flag conflicts if two details disagree.\n        - **Beam / Sloof Total Length Calculation by Segment Summation**:\n          - Never use building perimeter as total beam/sloof length.\n          - Identify individual beam/sloof segments along grid lines, group by code (`S.1`, `B1`, `B2`, etc.), avoid double-counting shared intersections, sum all segments, and display a structured **Tabel Rincian Segmen** (`Tipe | Segmen / Grid | Panjang (m) | Total`) before/when applying to the calculator.\n          - Test specifically against the attached user PDF: `/public/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf` (Page 1: `DENAH SLOOF` Scale 1:200 + `TABEL DIMENSI & POTONGAN SLOOF S.1` with width `l = 40 cm` (0.40 m) and height `t = 60 cm` (0.60 m), horizontal & vertical `S.1` segments on grids A\342\200\223H and 1\342\200\2238).\n     6. **Floor-Grouped Work Addition & Multi-Select**:\n        - Keep `+ Tambah Pekerjaan` per floor group and multi-select in `AddWorkModal.tsx`.\n     7. **Clean UI Without USC / Excel Cell Leaks**:\n        - Never show USC names, Excel filenames, sheet names, cell addresses, or raw Excel formulas in the UI.\n     8. **Final Report**:\n        - Report modified files, implemented features, tested features, test results using `/public/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf`, any remaining issues, and any external Firebase Console configuration note (e.g., if enabling Email/Password provider in Firebase Console is needed alongside Google Sign-In).\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Previously**:\n     - `server.ts`: Added JSON error middleware, 50MB payload support, `Content-Type: application/json` enforcement, and Gemini retry/fallback logic.\n     - `src/components/AutoQuantityTakeoffSection.tsx`: Created side-by-side compact cards for **Asisten AI \342\200\224 Auto Quantity Takeoff** (with **\"Coba Sekarang\"** button opening `AIAssistantModal`) and **Input Manual** (with **\"Buka Form Input\"** button).\n     - `src/components/RightPanel.tsx`: Removed duplicate AI Assistant card from the right panel.\n     - `src/components/WorkTable.tsx`: Added per-floor `+ Tambah Pekerjaan` buttons and status filters.\n     - `src/components/AddWorkModal.tsx`: Added multi-select checkboxes and bulk add to target floor.\n   - **Completed in Current Turn (Firebase Setup Flow)**:\n     - Read `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` and `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`.\n     - Called `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"` and waited for user confirmation.\n     - User accepted Firebase terms (`user_confirmed_in_ui: true`).\n     - Called `rpc_action` with `service_name: \"fax\"`, `method_name: \"GetFirebaseTos\"`, which returned `{\"accepted\": true}`.\n   - **In Progress (IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTION)**:\n     - Must immediately call `rpc_action` with `service_name: \"fax\"`, `method_name: \"ProvisionFirebase\"`, `arguments: { platform: \"web\" }` as required by `firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` before writing Firebase code.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Attached Test Document (`/public/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf`)**:\n     - Contains **Page 1: DENAH SLOOF (Skala 1:200)** and a **Tabel Dimensi & Potongan Sloof** on the same sheet.\n     - The table specifies `TIPE SLOOF: S.1`, `DIMENSI: l = 40, t = 60` (40 cm \303\227 60 cm = 0.40 m \303\227 0.60 m), Tulangan Atas `4 D22`, Tulangan Tengah `2 D12`, Tulangan Bawah `4 D22`, Sengkang `\303\23010-100` (tumpuan) / `\303\23010-150` (lapangan), Selimut beton `5 cm`.\n     - The plan (`DENAH SLOOF`) shows grid lines `A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H` horizontally (`6.00`, `6.00`, `0.50`, `3.00`, `2.20`, `2.30` -> total width `20.00 m`) and `1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8` vertically (`3.60`, `2.40`, `1.00`, `3.00`, `3.00`, `12.00`, `1.50` -> main vertical span `25.00 m` + `1.50 m` drop-off/entrance projection), with `S.1` segments labeled along the grid spans.\n   - **Firebase Auth & Backend Isolation**:\n     - Per `firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md`, `ProvisionFirebase` provisions Firestore Enterprise Edition and Google Auth (`firebase-applet-config.json`).\n     - We should install `firebase` via `install_applet_package` and also provide full support for Email/Password + Google Sign-In (`signInWithPopup`) plus a hardened server-backed/Firestore-backed user & project store so both Create Account (with Full Name, Email, Password, Role: `Student | Estimator | Other`) and Sign In work seamlessly out of the box even if Email/Password provider hasn\'t been manually toggled in the Firebase console yet, while syncing to Firestore when authenticated.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - Earlier issue `Unexpected token \'<\', \"<!doctype \"... is not valid JSON` was fixed in `server.ts` and `AIAssistantModal.tsx` by adding Express error-handling middleware and checking `response.headers.get(\'content-type\')` before calling `response.json()`.\n   - Upstream Gemini API occasionally returns `503 Service Unavailable` under high load; handled with retry + model fallback (`gemini-3.8-flash` -> `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` -> `gemini-flash-latest`) in `server.ts`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on port 3000.\n   - User email in metadata: `muh.bima.adjie@gmail.com`.\n   - `GetFirebaseTos` has already returned `{\"accepted\": true}`.\n\n6. **Next Steps (Priority Order)**\n   1. **Provision Firebase**:\n      - Call `rpc_action` with `service_name: \"fax\"`, `method_name: \"ProvisionFirebase\"`, `arguments: { platform: \"web\" }`.\n      - Install `firebase` package (and `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules` if needed) via `install_applet_package`.\n   2. **Firebase Blueprint, Security Rules & Connection**:\n      - Create `firebase-blueprint.json`, `security_spec.md`, `firestore.rules`, and deploy rules via `rpc_action` (`service_name: \"fax\"`, `method_name: \"DeployRules\"`).\n      - Create `src/firebase.ts` loading `firebase-applet-config.json` and calling `getDocFromServer(doc(db, \'test\', \'connection\'))` on boot, plus `handleFirestoreError`.\n   3. **Authentication System & User Profile (`src/services/authService.ts`, `src/components/AuthPage.tsx`, `src/components/UserProfileModal.tsx`)**:\n      - Implement Sign In & Create Account page (Full Name, Email, Password, Confirm Password, User Type: `Student`, `Estimator`, `Other`, Show/Hide Password, Forgot Password modal, Google Sign-In + Email/Password auth with backend `/api/auth/*` + Firestore sync so registration & login always succeed reliably with password hashing (`crypto.scryptSync`) and token/session verification).\n      - Update `Header.tsx` to display the logged-in user\'s name, email, role (`Student` / `Estimator` / `Other`), initials avatar, profile settings, and Logout button (removing hardcoded \"Adjie\").\n      - Add a **User Dashboard / Projects Hub** view upon login (or via \"Proyek\" nav) showing personalized greeting, project count, last opened project, \"Buat Proyek Baru\" CTA, and isolated user project list.\n   4. **Default Project & Standardized Catalog (`src/data/uscCatalog.ts`, `src/services/projectStorage.ts`)**:\n      - Change default project creation for new users to `\"Proyek Baru\"` with empty work list (or optional standard empty works) and **zero USC demo dimensions**. Preserve existing projects in storage without deleting them.\n      - Update `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS` in `src/data/uscCatalog.ts` to include generic structural items (`Kolom K1`, `Kolom K2`, `Kolom K3`, `Kolom Praktis`, `Kolom Kustom`, `Balok B1`, `Balok B2`, `Balok B3`, `Balok Induk`, `Balok Anak`, `Balok Bordes`, `Ring Balok`, `Balok Kustom`, `Sloof S1`, `Sloof S2`, `Sloof S3`, `Sloof Kustom`, `Pondasi Tapak`, `Pondasi Batu Kali`, `Plat Lantai`, `Plat Tangga`, `Tangga Beton`, `Dinding Bata Ringan`, etc.) with `value: null` for all dimensions and clean labels (no `50 x 50 cm` or USC references).\n   5. **Vertical Parameter Input Form (`src/components/WorkDetailModal.tsx`)**:\n      - Redesign parameter inputs into a clean vertical/grid card layout where each parameter has its bold label above the input field, unit badge, informative placeholder (`Masukkan panjang total (m)`), required indicator, live formula display, and automatic volume result box.\n   6. **Multi-Type Drawing AI & Segment Summation for Beam/Sloof (`server.ts`, `src/components/AIAssistantModal.tsx`, `src/services/projectStorage.ts`, `src/types/index.ts`)**:\n      - Enhance `/api/gemini/extract-dimensions` in `server.ts` and `AIAssistantModal.tsx` to:\n        - Classify each page/region into the 13 drawing types (`denah_arsitektur`, `denah_kolom`, `denah_balok`, `denah_sloof`, `denah_pondasi`, `potongan_bangunan`, `tampak_bangunan`, `detail_tangga`, `detail_pondasi`, `detail_sambungan`, `detail_penulangan`, `tabel_dimensi_penulangan`, `detail_konstruksi_lainnya`).\n        - Extract and group **Beam / Sloof Segments** (`segments: [{ elementCode, segmentName, gridLocation, rawLength, convertedLengthM }]`) so total length is calculated as the exact sum of identified segments (never building perimeter).\n        - Cross-link element codes across regions/pages (e.g., `S.1` segments from `Denah Sloof` + `S.1` width `40 cm` & height `60 cm` from `Tabel Dimensi dan Penulangan` on `/public/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf` -> `Sloof S1` with `lebar = 0.40 m`, `tinggi = 0.60 m`, and `panjang_total = sum of S.1 segments`).\n        - Display the multi-region classification badges and the **Tabel Rincian Segmen Balok / Sloof** (`Tipe | Segmen | Lokasi Grid | Panjang`) inside `AIAssistantModal.tsx` and `WorkDetailModal.tsx`.\n        - Provide a quick-load test button in `AIAssistantModal.tsx` for `Gedung_USC_A4-16.pdf` (`/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf`) so the user can test it with 1 click.\n   7. **Verification**:\n      - Test `/api/gemini/extract-dimensions` and segment calculation against `/public/assets/aistudio/Gedung_USC_A4-16_202766c9.pdf`.\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to ensure zero errors.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Do not rebuild from scratch or remove existing working features.\n   - Never expose USC demo data as default values for new projects or catalog items.\n   - Never expose Excel filenames, sheet names, cell coordinates, or raw Excel formulas in the UI.\n   - Follow `firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` strictly: call `ProvisionFirebase` first before writing Firebase code.\n</summary>"
