  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Prompt Requirements**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting the user\'s prompt, pinpointing every requirement. I\'m focusing on ensuring absolute accuracy and comprehensive implementation of each point, especially the changes to product identity (`RuangRAB` to `Ruang`). I am moving from the general to the specific, and focusing on thoroughness. I\'m making sure to go back and forth between parts to make sure they all work together.\n\n\n**Adjusting Application Identity**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in updating all application identifiers. I\'ve successfully adjusted the app name on the login page, the logo and identity within the dashboard, page titles, and even the product name on the user profile, AI Assistant display and exported Excel files, as well as every visible instance of the app. The product description is implemented. I\'m focusing on ensuring zero remaining instances of the old name.\n\n\n**Generating Default Work Items**\n\nI\'m now focused on the automated generation of standard work item lists. My current approach involves leveraging existing catalog structures but stripping out project-specific details such as dimensions and calculations. I\'m focusing on defining default work groups, starting with \"Umum & Pondasi\" and its constituent items. I\'m ensuring all numerical values are null. I\'m implementing the detailed structure for each floor, starting with \"fl-umum\". I am making sure the automated generation is comprehensive and accurate.\n\n\n**Defining Work Item Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of work items. I\'m focusing on defining default details for various structural components. Currently, I\'m working through the components for the first floor (\"fl-1\"), including columns, beams, slabs, walls, and finishing. I\'m making sure these items are comprehensive, from \"Pasangan Batu Kosong\" to \"Pengecatan Dinding Interior\". I\'m meticulously detailing each element.\n\n\n**Expanding Work Item Definitions**\n\nI\'m now expanding the work item definitions to include more detailed specifications. I\'m focusing on the first floor\'s finishing and mechanical, electrical, and plumbing (MEP) items. I\'m meticulously detailing items like \"Pasangan Lantai Homogenous Tile 60x60\" and \"Instalasi Titik Lampu & Saklar\" with the appropriate code. I am making sure the second floor and beyond follow a similar standardized structure.\n\n\n**Implementing Work Item Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing new item features, focusing on user interaction and data handling. I\'ve ensured null values for all parameters, making sure the formulas calculate automatically once the user inputs data, allowing for flexibility. I\'m focusing on the implementation of delete functionality with a confirmation modal, and am including the new multi-select deletion feature with checkboxes and a floating action bar. I am planning on adding a \"Recently Deleted\" list.\n\n\n**Refining Work Item Functions**\n\nI\'m now refining the work item functions based on user requirements. I\'m focusing on providing an \"Undo/Redo Last Deleted Work Item\" feature with a \"Reload Floor Standard Work Items\" button. I\'m also adding the ability to edit work item names and parameters directly within `WorkDetailModal.tsx`. I am ensuring that deleting items in one project doesn\'t affect the global standard catalog.\n\nI am also focusing on implementing manual work item additions, with \"+\" buttons in each section, and multi-select functionality for adding multiple items at once. Finally, I\'m working on automatic work item group generation when a new floor is added.\n\n\n**Managing Floor Workflows**\n\nI\'m now implementing new floor management features with confirmation modals in `FloorManagementModal.tsx`, addressing both data transfer and deletion workflows. I\'m focusing on ensuring all project data integrity with careful handling of user deletion and data separation. I am ensuring that manual and AI-generated items work together, as well.\n\n\n**Updating AI Quantity Logic**\n\nI\'m now revising the AI\'s quantity estimation logic to refine how it interacts with existing default work items. I\'m focusing on ensuring the AI *updates* parameters of existing items (based on `catalogId` and `dedupKey`), instead of generating duplicates. I\'m specifically working on the `applyAutoQuantityTakeoff` function in `src/services/projectStorage.ts` to implement this deduplication strategy and verification status updates. I am ensuring that work items are only flagged for user verification (`\'draft\'`) if the AI makes changes.\n\n\n**Clarifying Work Item Status**\n\nI\'m now integrating clearer status indicators within the work item list (`WorkTable.tsx`). I\'m focusing on displaying statuses like \"Belum Diisi,\" \"Tidak Lengkap,\" \"Perlu Verifikasi,\" and \"Terverifikasi\" to guide the user. I\'m making sure that incomplete items don\'t contribute to the final calculated volume. I\'m making it easy to identify missing parameters.\n\n\n"
