  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing File Context**\n\nI\'ve examined `index.html` and `metadata.json`. The user wants to update the product identity and description to \"RuangEstimasi \342\200\224 Platform AI Quantity Takeoff untuk membantu membaca gambar teknik\". I\'m now figuring out the best way to integrate these changes within the existing project structure and ensure compatibility.\n\n\n**Refining Identity Updates**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific file modifications. Considering user instructions and environmental constraints, I\'ll update the application identity throughout `index.html`, including the title and Open Graph tags, and the application description in both `index.html` and `metadata.json`. It looks like the system rule of \"never rename\" means I will leave `name` alone. The update applies specifically to the description in `metadata.json`. I\'m focusing on seamless integration and consistent application of these changes across the defined areas.\n\n\n**Implementing Core Changes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core changes. Specifically, I\'m updating `<title>`, `<meta name=\"description\">`, `og:title`, and `og:description` in `index.html`, and the `description` field in `metadata.json` to reflect the updated RuangEstimasi information.  I\'m also preparing for the next set of changes, checking requirement 5: \"Tampilkan status pekerjaan: - Belum Diisi\". I\'m making sure these updates are carefully sequenced to ensure a smooth transition.\n\n\n**Defining Calculation Statuses**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new calculation statuses. I\'ve updated `CalculationStatus` in `src/types/index.ts` to include `\'Belum Diisi\'`, `\'Tidak Lengkap\'`, `\'Perlu Verifikasi\'`, and `\'Terverifikasi\'`, ensuring backwards compatibility. In `calculateWorkItemVolume`, I\'m implementing logic to prevent final volume calculation if required parameters are missing or unfilled. If the filled count is zero, I\'ll set the status appropriately. I\'m focusing on providing users with clear indicators of incomplete work.\n\n\n**Implementing Status Details**\n\nI\'m now refining the status messaging for work items.  I\'ll ensure clear user guidance by dynamically crafting specific messages based on calculation completeness. If required parameters are missing (`\'Belum Diisi\'`), I\'ll provide a message directing the user to complete dimensions.  If only some parameters are missing (`\'Tidak Lengkap\'`), I\'ll list the missing ones. When calculations are possible, I\'ll then set the status to \"Perlu Verifikasi\" if it is from the AI, otherwise \"Terverifikasi\".\n\n\n**Calculating Status Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating more nuanced status metrics. I\'m defining completed, unfilled, incomplete, and verification-needed works based on specific status conditions. I\'m focusing on accurately categorizing work items, and I\'ll include logic to add `calculatedVolume` to various totals only when the work is verified, or when the work is complete. I\'ll need to remember to update project storage and catalog based on AI results.\n\n\n**Generating Default Works**\n\nI\'m now implementing the default works generation. Specifically, I am defining the default work items to be generated for the general and foundation floor levels. When the `floorId` is `\'fl-umum\'` or `floorLevel` is 0, the `createDefaultWorksForFloor` function will now populate a standard template from `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`, including items like `\'prep-pembersihan-lahan\'`, `\'str-galian-tanah-biasa-1m\'`, and several more. I am focusing on ensuring this default generation correctly populates the initial project structure.\n\n\n**Expanding Work Generation**\n\nI\'m now expanding the default work item generation to include floor-specific items. For floorLevel 0, I\'ll add `\'str-footplat-beton\'` and `\'str-sloof-beton\'`, and when `floorLevel >= 1`, I\'ll include items like `\'str-kolom-k1-beton\'` and `\'ars-keramik-toilet-antislip\'` from `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`. I\'m verifying the correct generation of building components for each floor level.\n\n\n\n**Adding Default Work Items**\n\nI\'m now integrating more default work items and refining the generation rules. I\'m expanding default work item generation for all floor levels to include new items such as: `ars-keramik-toilet-antislip`, `ars-plafond-gypsum-9mm`, `ars-pintu-kayu-engineering`, `ars-jendela-aluminium-kaca`, `mep-titik-lampu-nyy`, `mep-stop-kontak`, `mep-kloset-duduk`, and `mep-pipa-air-bersih-pvc`, across floorLevels. I\'m verifying proper cloning of parameters with null values and setting default states (status: `\'Belum Diisi\'`, `calculatedVolume: null`) and the dedup key. I\'m adding `str-ring-balok` to `floorLevel >= 2`.\n\n\n**Integrating Empty Project Logic**\n\nI\'m now incorporating logic to handle projects with no existing work items. In `loadAllProjects`, if a project retrieved from `localStorage` has an empty `works` array, I will use `createDefaultWorksForFloor` for each floor to populate its works. This ensures that even legacy projects start with a standard set of work items. I\'m focusing on providing a consistent initial state regardless of the project\'s origin.\n\n\n**Refining Update Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic for work item updates. When a catalog item match is found, I\'m checking if the `targetFloorId` already has that specific catalog item. If not, I\'m verifying if \'fl-umum\' contains an unfilled default work with that `catalogId`. Even if the target floor isn\'t \'fl-umum\' but the item is in \'fl-umum\', the system will now update the existing item to avoid duplication. The focus is on preventing duplicate entries.\n\n\n**Updating AI Takeoff Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the auto quantity takeoff updates. I\'ve ensured when `applyAutoQuantityTakeoff` updates existing default works, it only fills in parameters with clear AI evidence and leaves others `null`. Additionally, the new implementation checks to ensure work items are never duplicated, regardless of whether the target floor is \'fl-umum\' or not. This avoids duplicate work items. I\'m also setting `existingWork.origin = \'ai\'`, `existingWork.aiVerificationStatus = \'draft\'`, `existingWork.sourceDocument`, and `existingWork.identificationReason = firstUpdate?.reason`.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Work Table Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the multi-select deletion and status banner updates to the work table. I\'m adding a checkbox column for selecting items across floors and implementing a sticky bar. I am preparing to implement the explanatory banner, and the \"Muat Ulang Pekerjaan Standar\" button.\n\n\n**Implementing Action Bar**\n\nI\'m now implementing the work table action bar features. I\'m focusing on the multi-select deletion, and status badge integration. The action bar will display the number of selected works, with buttons to delete or deselect. I am also planning the integration of status badges and filter pills based on status. I will implement a \"Muat Ulang Pekerjaan Standar\" button.\n\nI am planning to implement an action bar and status badge updates to the work table. The action bar shows the number of selected works with the delete and cancel options.  I\'ll be adding the display status badges per row, and integrating filter pills. I plan to add the \"Muat Ulang Pekerjaan Standar\" button.\n\n\n**Adding Parameter Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating the parameter column updates within the `WorkTable.tsx`. If all work parameters are `null`, I will clearly display \"Kosong (Belum Diisi)\" to provide an immediate indicator to the user. Also, the Volume column will display \"\342\200\224\" when `calculatedVolume === null`.\n\nI\'m now integrating an editable **Nama Pekerjaan** input field at the top of `WorkDetailModal.tsx` so users can rename any work item in their project without affecting the global catalog. I will also be working on integrating Floor Management Modal features, specifically, floor addition and deletion features with default works.\n\n\n**Implementing Floor Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new floor management features. I\'ll automatically generate standard works for a newly added floor, and append these to the project. I\'m working to add a confirmation panel for the floor deletion action, with options to transfer the work items or completely delete the floor, including works, using a modal. I\'ll make sure to handle scenarios of empty floors as well.\n\n\n"
