  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Project Storage**\n\nI\'m currently modifying `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`. My focus is on ensuring all comments and branding within the file consistently reflect \"RuangEstimasi\". Additionally, I am incorporating the new constants `DEFAULT_UMUM_CATALOG_IDS`, `DEFAULT_FLOOR_1_CATALOG_IDS`, and `DEFAULT_UPPER_FLOOR_CATALOG_IDS` into the file\'s structure.\n\n\n**Defining Default Works**\n\nI\'ve begun outlining the default work items, specifically for the ground floor (`fl-umum` / `floorLevel === 0`). This includes preparatory tasks like site clearing and temporary fencing, along with foundational elements such as excavation, backfill, stone masonry, and footplate construction. The goal is to provide a comprehensive and pre-defined set of project works.\n\n\n**Listing Second Floor Works**\n\nI\'m now detailing the structural and architectural components for the first floor. This includes columns (K1, K2, practical columns), beams (main, secondary, B1, B2), the floor slab, and the staircase. I am also working on the wall details such as masonry, plastering, interior paint, flooring (homogenous tile, toilet ceramic), ceiling (gypsum), doors, and windows.\n\n\n**Defining Upper Floor Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing standard structure for the second floor and beyond. I\'ve noted that it\'s largely similar to the first floor, with the addition of `str-ring-balok`. Every work item generated by `createDefaultWorksForFloor` now has a standardized format for parameters, volume, status, and a `dedupKey`. Specifically, its status is initially \"Belum Diisi\". I have also considered the behavior of `createNewProject`, which now auto-populates \'works\' via `createDefaultWorksForFloor`, and the behavior in `loadAllProjects`.\n\n\n**Implementing AI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m currently working to integrate AI-driven quantity take-off into the project workflow. When AI extracts data with a `catalogId`, I\'m implementing logic to find and update the corresponding work items within the project. The search prioritizes the target floor, then checks for general or foundation items in the \'fl-umum\' floor. I\'m also addressing how to update work parameters, especially for AI drafts, to ensure they\'re appropriately marked and linked.\n\n\n"
