    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user wants to fix the standard work template source in **RuangEstimasi** (`# PERBAIKAN SUMBER TEMPLATE PEKERJAAN RUANGESTIMASI`):\n- **Core Problem Reported by User**: The previous implementation replaced/reduced the default template to a subset (`DEFAULT_UMUM_PONDASI_CATALOG_IDS`, `DEFAULT_LANTAI_1_CATALOG_IDS`, `DEFAULT_LANTAI_ATAS_CATALOG_IDS` in `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`) or deleted USC work templates while keeping user-created works. The user requires that the **complete USC building work catalog/reference** be used as the global standard template source for RuangEstimasi, NOT a simplified subset or only a few examples (like K1, K2, B1, B2).\n- **Key Deliverables & Success Criteria**:\n  1. **Restore USC Work Template (`## 1. PULIHKAN TEMPLATE PEKERJAAN USC`)**:\n     - Use the complete USC work catalog/reference as the primary source of the standard template, including:\n       - Kelompok Umum & Pondasi\n       - Kelompok pekerjaan Lantai 1\n       - Kelompok pekerjaan Lantai 2\n       - Kelompok lantai lainnya jika tersedia dalam referensi\n       - Pekerjaan Persiapan, Struktural, Arsitektural, dan MEP (jika tersedia)\n       - All work types and variations present in the USC catalog/reference.\n     - Preserve original valid work names, categories, units, parameter definitions, and formulas (`excelSheet`, `excelCell`, `excelFormula`, `formulaDisplay`, `calculationMethod`).\n  2. **Clear All USC Demonstration Values (`## 2. KOSONGKAN SELURUH NILAI DEMONSTRASI USC`)**:\n     - The USC template is used ONLY for work structure, parameter definitions, units, and formulas.\n     - All dimensions, lengths, widths, heights, thicknesses, element counts, areas, volumes, parameter values (`value: null`), calculation results (`calculatedVolume: null`), and old verification statuses must be cleared on new project copies.\n     - Initial status of all copied template works must be `\"Belum Diisi\"`.\n  3. **Preserve User Project Data (`## 3. JANGAN HAPUS DATA PROYEK PENGGUNA`)**:\n     - Never delete user projects, custom works created by users, or valid project parameters.\n     - Do not overwrite existing user project data with the USC template or delete works just because they are not in the USC catalog.\n  4. **Separate Global Template & Project Data (`## 4. PISAHKAN TEMPLATE GLOBAL DAN DATA PROYEK`)**:\n     - **A. Global Standard Template**: Sourced from the full USC catalog (work name, floor group, category, unit, formula, parameter definitions; zero project dimensions).\n     - **B. User Project Data**: Independent copy of works from the global template when a project is created, with independent parameters/volumes, editable/deletable without affecting the global template or other projects, and supporting custom works.\n  5. **New Projects Must Use Full USC Template (`## 5. PROYEK BARU HARUS MENGGUNAKAN TEMPLATE USC`)**:\n     - Creating a new project copies the full USC work structure into the new project with all parameters `null`, `calculatedVolume: null`, and status `\"Belum Diisi\"`.\n  6. **Data Migration & Recovery (`## 6. MIGRASI DAN PEMULIHAN DATA`)**:\n     - Before modifying: inspect stored USC template sources (e.g., `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts`, `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`, git history if any, or other files), inspect current work catalog, inspect user project data/migration logic in `projectStorage.ts`, identify custom works, and check if any USC reference data was overwritten or removed.\n     - Restore the USC template from available reference sources in the project if possible. Do NOT fabricate a fake USC catalog if the original source is missing (report if original source needs re-importing, or restore from git/codebase if present).\n  7. **Verification (`## 7. PENGUJIAN`)**:\n     - Verify all 10 checklist items from section 7 of the prompt.\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Previous Turn (before the new user request)**:\n  - Renamed product branding from `RuangRAB` to `RuangEstimasi` across UI, `metadata.json`, `index.html`, `server.ts`, `src/components/AIAssistantModal.tsx`, and `src/services/projectStorage.ts`.\n  - Verified build (`compile_applet`) and TypeScript (`lint_applet`) passed with 0 errors.\n- **Completed in Current Turn (for the new user request)**:\n  - Listed `/src/data` (contains `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts`).\n  - Inspected `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223941 of 1621 lines).\n  - Inspected `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223300 of 1337 lines).\n- **In Progress / Not Yet Inspected**:\n  - Need to read `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` (since the metadata notes the app has a Firestore DB `ai-studio-ruangrabaiquanti-fe31a1d6-62db-405b-8277-2f5da668fc00` and `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` imports `../firebase`).\n  - Need to view the rest of `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` (lines 940\342\200\2231621) and `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` (lines 900\342\200\2231337) to see all items currently in `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS` and how project creation/migration (`migrateLegacyProjects` / `createNewProject` / `createDefaultWorksForFloor`) currently works.\n  - Need to check git history (`git log`, `git status`, `git diff` via `run_command`) or any other files in the workspace to see if an earlier version of `uscCatalog.ts` or `projectStorage.ts` had the full original Gedung USC work list and floor assignments before `DEFAULT_UMUM_PONDASI_CATALOG_IDS` / `DEFAULT_LANTAI_1_CATALOG_IDS` were introduced.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- In `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` (lines 47\342\200\223114):\n  - Currently, `DEFAULT_UMUM_PONDASI_CATALOG_IDS` (17 items), `DEFAULT_LANTAI_1_CATALOG_IDS` (21 items), and `DEFAULT_LANTAI_ATAS_CATALOG_IDS` (22 items) only pick a subset of IDs from `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`!\n  - Even within `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` (lines 1\342\200\223941 viewed so far), there are many more USC catalog items that were excluded from those arrays (for example: `str-sloof-s3`, `str-sloof-kustom`, `str-kolom-k3-beton`, `str-kolom-kustom`, `str-kolom-k1-tulangan`, `str-kolom-k1-bekisting`, `str-balok-b3-beton`, `str-balok-bordes`, `str-balok-kustom`, `str-balok-b1-tulangan`, plus items in lines 941\342\200\2231621 not yet viewed).\n  - Furthermore, we should check git history (`git log -p` or `git log --stat`) to see if an earlier commit in the repo contained the original Gedung USC project/catalog structure (e.g., `createInitialUSCProject` or original `uscCatalog.ts`) that had the exact USC floor groupings (Umum & Pondasi, Lantai 1, Lantai 2, etc.) and work items.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier in the session (prior to the new user prompt), inline `npx tsx -e` verification scripts had minor import name mismatches (`recalculateProjectWorks` -> `recalculateAllProjectWorks`, `USC_CATALOG` -> `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`, `createWorkItemFromCatalog` -> `createProjectWorkFromCatalog`, `parameterLabel` -> `parameterName`). All were resolved and all 9 checks passed.\n- No build or lint errors exist currently (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet` both succeeded).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running cleanly on port 3000.\n- No background tasks are running.\n- `src/services/projectStorage.ts` uses both `localStorage` and Firebase Firestore (`db`).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Skill Check Requirement**: Call `view_file` on `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` first (blocking requirement from system prompt when interacting with code that uses Firebase/Firestore).\n2. **Inspect Remaining Files & Git History**:\n   - View lines 940\342\200\2231621 of `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` to see all items currently in `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`.\n   - View lines 900\342\200\2231337 of `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` to inspect `createNewProject`, `loadUserProjects`, `migrateLegacyProjects`, and how existing user projects and legacy USC demo projects were handled.\n   - Run `git log -n 10 --stat` (via `run_command`) to check if git history has the original USC catalog/project definition so we can see every single USC work item and floor group without fabricating anything.\n3. **Restore Complete USC Standard Template & Floor Groupings**:\n   - Ensure `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` contains the complete, authentic USC work catalog (Persiapan Dll, Struktural, Arsitektural, MEP across Umum & Pondasi, Lantai 1, Lantai 2, etc.) with all original formulas, units, categories, Excel references (`excelSheet`, `excelCell`, `excelFormula`), and parameter definitions, while keeping all default parameter `value: null`.\n   - Update `createDefaultWorksForFloor` / `createNewProject` in `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` so that new projects (and floor template loading) copy the **entire** USC standard work template for each floor group (`floorRule: \'umum\' | \'fondasi_saja\'` for Umum & Pondasi, and all `floorRule: \'per_lantai\'` or floor-specific USC works for Lantai 1, Lantai 2, etc.) rather than filtering down to a tiny hardcoded subset.\n   - Ensure all copied works in a new project have `value: null` on every parameter, `calculatedVolume: null`, `status: \'Belum Diisi\'`, and no leftover USC demo numbers.\n4. **Preserve User Projects & Custom Works During Migration/Loading**:\n   - Check `loadUserProjects` / migration logic in `/src/services/projectStorage.ts` to ensure existing user projects, custom works, and user-entered parameters are NEVER deleted or overwritten when loading projects.\n   - Ensure strict deep-cloning/isolation between the global USC template (`CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS`), `Proyek A`, and `Proyek B`.\n5. **Run Full Verification Suite (10 Checks)**:\n   - Write and run a verification script testing all 10 items in `## 7. PENGUJIAN`.\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to verify zero build or TypeScript errors.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Never fabricate USC catalog items**: Restore from existing codebase/git reference; if any original USC source is missing, report honestly.\n- **Never delete user project data**: Existing user projects and custom works must remain intact.\n- **Zero demo values in new projects**: Every work in a newly created project must start with `null` parameters, `null` volume, and status `\"Belum Diisi\"`.\n</summary>"
