    thinking: "**Analyzing the Codebase**\n\nI\'m now carefully analyzing the codebase, paying close attention to the user\'s request regarding `# PERBAIKAN SUMBER TEMPLATE PEKERJAAN RUANGESTIMASI`. My focus is on understanding the context of the issue. Also, I\'m reviewing the audit findings of `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` to see how it relates to this.\n\n\n**Exploring USC Catalog Details**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the specifics of `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts`. I\'ve found 75 work items categorized across eight sections. Each item has detailed metadata from the USC Excel reference, including formulas and unit information, which looks to be valid. Now, I\'m checking for any further USC work items or default values within the catalog.\n\n\n**Identifying Default Values**\n\nI\'m now thoroughly examining `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts`, specifically focusing on entries with non-null `value:` properties. I\'ve noted a list of default values, as described above, such as the `jumlah_kolom` with a value of 1, and various dimensions, areas, and quantities set to zero, such as `panjang_bengkokan`, `luas_bukaan`, `luas_bordes`, and various light fixtures. Also, I\'m now referencing the prompt regarding clearing the USC demonstration values, where dimensions, quantities, and results need to be emptied.\n\n\n**Clarifying Value Handling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `createProjectWorkFromCatalog` function. I\'m making sure every parameter gets set to `value: null` when a work item is created from the catalog, *especially* when `initialParameterValues` isn\'t passed. This means no default values, not even zero, will be pre-filled. Also, I\'m verifying that every parameter in `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS` also has `value: null` within `uscCatalog.ts`. I want to make certain no \"demo\" values remain by default.\n\n\n**Reviewing Project Storage**\n\nI\'m now diving into `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`, specifically focusing on the previous implementation. I noticed the old method created hardcoded, small arrays of default catalog IDs for new projects and floors. These included `DEFAULT_UMUM_PONDASI_CATALOG_IDS`, `DEFAULT_LANTAI_1_CATALOG_IDS`, and `DEFAULT_LANTAI_ATAS_CATALOG_IDS`. This implementation used only a small fraction of the available 75 items in `uscCatalog.ts`, and I\'ve started listing some of the excluded items like \'prep-direksi-keet\' and \'prep-pagar-sementara\'.\n\n\n**Listing Excluded Items**\n\nI\'m now identifying additional excluded items, extending the previous list. This includes items like `papan-nama`, `prep-mobilisasi`, `prep-k3`, and various foundation-related tasks. I\'m noting each in detail to ensure no items are unintentionally defaulted in new projects.\n\n\n**Listing Further Exclusions**\n\nI\'m now cataloging even more omitted items from the default lists. This includes numerous foundation, structural, and concrete work components like \'pondasi-footplat-kustom\', \'str-sloof-s3\', \'str-balok-kustom\', and many others. It\'s becoming clear that nearly half of the items in `CATALOG_WORK_ITEMS` were excluded in the previous project storage implementation.\n\n\n**Uncovering Migration Issues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the legacy project migration process, specifically within `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`. I\'ve identified that the code filters out the \"Gedung USC\" project (and its contents) during the migration from `LEGACY_STORAGE_KEY_PROJECTS` (ruangrab_projects_v1), effectively deleting it from local storage. This leaves the user with either a new or simplified project. I need to consider how to handle this data loss in an upgrade.\n\n\n**Confirming Data Deletion**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the user\'s observation: the system was indeed deleting the \"Gedung USC\" project during migration. The `loadAllProjects` function was filtering out `proj-gedung-usc` and its associated data from local storage. Furthermore, the simplified `DEFAULT_*_CATALOG_IDS` arrays in `createDefaultWorksForFloor` were used, not the complete USC catalog, resulting in incomplete project creation. I\'m now certain this is the root cause of the data loss.\n\n\n"
