  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 8
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Apply the \"MASTER PROMPT PERBAIKAN \342\200\224 RUANGESTIMASI: Isolasi Data Pengguna, Tampilan Kategori Pekerjaan, dan Optimalisasi AI Quantity Takeoff\" to the existing **RuangEstimasi** application without rebuilding from scratch or removing existing features.\n   - **Three Primary Deliverables**:\n     1. **Perbaikan Data Demo dan Isolasi Antarakun (Section 1)**:\n        - Audit all storage sources (Firestore DB, server storage, seed data, default project, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, React state, cache, AI analysis results, project creation, login/user data loading).\n        - Find and eliminate any source of legacy/demo values such as `12.7` m (panjang lahan), `6` m (lebar lahan), `76.20` m\302\262 (volume pembersihan lahan), `37.40` m (panjang bouwplank), or stale AI extraction data from previous uploads.\n        - Enforce strict per-user and per-project isolation:\n          - Every user has their own projects; Account A cannot read, modify, or delete Account B\'s data.\n          - Every project has its own parameters, calculated volumes, and AI extraction results bound to `(userId, projectId)`.\n          - Do not rely solely on `localStorage` as the only persistence mechanism; enforce ownership checks on backend/database (server-side API & Firestore rules / storage).\n          - Distinguish global read-only `USC_STANDARD_TEMPLATE` from user project instances.\n          - Clean up demo/seed data without deleting real user-created projects. New projects must have all USC works with empty (`null`) parameters, `null` volumes, `Belum Diisi` status, and no AI data from previous documents.\n     2. **Sistem Kategori Pekerjaan Seperti Laci / Accordion (Section 2)**:\n        - Within each floor group (`Umum & Pondasi`, `Lantai 1`, `Lantai 2`, etc.), group works into collapsible category drawers (e.g., `Persiapan Dll` / `Struktural` / `Arsitektural` / `MEP`, following USC catalog categories).\n        - Each category has its own independent expand/collapse toggle (`\342\226\266 Kategori (N pekerjaan)` when collapsed, `\342\226\274 Kategori (N pekerjaan)` when expanded) plus an indicator of unfilled works (`Belum Diisi`).\n        - Opening one category MUST NOT open or close other categories.\n        - Category open/close state must be tracked independently per floor (`floorId + category`), so switching floors preserves each floor\'s accordion state.\n        - Provide **Show All** (opens all categories on the currently viewed floor) and **Minimalis** (closes all categories on the currently viewed floor) buttons. These only affect view state, never calculation or data.\n     3. **Optimalisasi Asisten AI Quantity Takeoff (Section 3)**:\n        - **Page/Segment Classification**: Classify every page/region into at least the 16 required types: `Denah arsitektur`, `Denah struktur`, `Denah pondasi`, `Denah kolom`, `Denah balok`, `Denah sloof`, `Denah pembesian`, `Gambar potongan`, `Gambar tampak`, `Detail konstruksi`, `Detail penulangan`, `Tabel dimensi atau schedule`, `Gambar tangga`, `Gambar atap`, `Gambar MEP`, `Tidak diketahui / perlu pemeriksaan manual`.\n        - **Page & Drawing Type Separation**: Each extracted item must record `pageNumber`, `drawingType`, `drawingTitle`, `floor`, `gridCode`, `elementCode`, `dimensions`, `unit`, and `sourceInfo`. Do not mix architectural plan dimensions with structural sections/schedules unless element identity (`elementCode`, `grid`, `floor`) matches.\n        - **Unit & Scale**: Support `mm`, `cm`, `m` and drawing scale without double-multiplying written dimensions. Never guess unreadable dimensions.\n        - **Total Length of Beams (Balok) & Sloof**: Calculate total length from the sum of identified grid segments (`Segmen A\342\200\223B: 3,00 m`, etc.) per element code (`B1`, `B2`, `S1`, etc.), avoiding double-counting at intersections and never substituting building perimeter for beam/sloof length. Show segment breakdown for user inspection.\n        - **Structural Schedule Matching**: Match `elementCode` (`K1`, `B1`, `S1`, etc.) between plans and structural tables/schedules (cross-section dimensions & reinforcement). Never use `B2` dimensions for `B1`.\n        - **USC Default Work Linking**: Map AI findings to existing USC standard works in the project first; only add a new work if the element is genuinely found in the drawing and not yet present; never duplicate works; place in the right floor & category.\n        - **Inspectable Source & Verification Status**: Every AI parameter must show its source (e.g. `Halaman 4, Denah Balok Lantai 1`) and distinct verification badge (`Terbaca Jelas`, `Hasil Penggabungan`, `Perlu Verifikasi`, `Tidak Ditemukan`). Never mark all AI results as `Terverifikasi` automatically. Allow user to edit, accept, or reject AI proposals.\n        - **Performance & Stability**: Avoid resending identical pages/images, add content/hash caching per page/document scoped to `(userId, projectId)`, display clear reading progress, support staged/per-page processing or fallback, limited retry for transient errors, and distinguish API error / unreadable file / unsupported format / incomplete extraction.\n   - **Target Metadata**:\n     - Applet ID: `fe31a1d6-62db-405b-8277-2f5da668fc00`\n     - User Email: `muh.bima.adjie@gmail.com`\n     - Firestore DB: `ai-studio-ruangrabaiquanti-fe31a1d6-62db-405b-8277-2f5da668fc00`\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in Earlier Turns**:\n     - Restored full 114-item `USC_STANDARD_TEMPLATE` in `/src/data/uscCatalog.ts` (`USC_CATALOG_VERSION = \'3.0.0-USC-FULL\'`) with `value: null` on all parameters.\n     - Fixed dev server cold-start in `/server.ts` so `app.listen(PORT, \'0.0.0.0\')` binds immediately while `createViteServer` initializes asynchronously. Verified `http://localhost:3000/` and `http://localhost:3000/api/health` return HTTP 200.\n   - **Completed in Current Turn**:\n     - Read required skills:\n       - `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md`\n       - `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md`\n       - `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`\n   - **In Progress / Next**:\n     - Need to read `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/3_saas_dashboard.md` (mandatory per `frontend-design` skill Section 4).\n     - Need to inspect the codebase files (`/src/App.tsx`, `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`, `/src/services/authService.ts`, `/src/services/aiService.ts` or similar, `/src/types.ts`, `/firestore.rules`, `/firebase-applet-config.json`, `/data/*`) to locate any `12.7`, `6`, `76.20`, `37.40` demo values, audit storage/auth/Firestore/server persistence, implement the accordion category UI, and upgrade the AI Quantity Takeoff pipeline.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - `/server.ts` currently stores users in `/data/users_store.json` (`/api/auth/register`, `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/update-profile`, `/api/auth/reset-password`) and provides `/api/gemini/extract-dimensions`.\n   - `package.json` already has `firebase` (`^13.2.0`), `express`, `@google/genai`, `exceljs`, `lucide-react`.\n   - The user reported seeing values `12,7` m, `6` m, `76,20` m\302\262, `37,40` m and previous AI extraction results across two different accounts. We must search all files in `/src` and `/data` for `12.7`, `37.4`, `76.2`, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, AI state, and Firestore/backend storage to find where demo values or unscoped storage keys exist.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Dev Server Cold-Start Timeout**: Earlier, the dev server didn\'t start in time because `await createViteServer` ran before `app.listen(3000)`. Fixed in `/server.ts` by binding `app.listen` immediately and awaiting `viteReady` in middleware. Verified with `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and `curl`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running cleanly on port 3000.\n   - No background tasks are running.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Read Mandatory Domain Reference**:\n      - Call `view_file` on `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/3_saas_dashboard.md`.\n   2. **Audit Codebase & Storage Sources (Section 1A)**:\n      - List files in `/src` and `/data` using `list_dir` and view `/src/types.ts`, `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`, `/src/App.tsx`, and any auth/AI/firebase files (`firebase-applet-config.json`, `firestore.rules`, etc.).\n      - Find where `12.7`, `6`, `76.20`, `37.40`, or AI fallback/mock/cached extraction results live (check `aiService`, `server.ts`, `projectStorage.ts`, `App.tsx`, `localStorage` keys, etc.).\n   3. **Implement User Data Isolation & Backend/Database Ownership Enforcement (Section 1B\342\200\2231D)**:\n      - Ensure all projects and AI extraction histories are strictly scoped to the authenticated `userId` both in client storage (`localStorage` namespaced by `userId`) AND backed by server/database persistence (`/api/projects` endpoints in `server.ts` + Firestore if configured, with strict `userId` ownership verification on every read/write/delete request).\n      - Automatically strip any legacy demo/seed values (`12.7`, `6`, `76.20`, `37.40`) when derived from old demo seeds while preserving legitimate user-created projects.\n      - Ensure AI Takeoff state (`extractionItems`, `segments`, `detectedRegions`, uploaded file preview, metadata) in React state and storage is bound to `(userId, activeProjectId)` and resets cleanly when switching projects or logging out/in as another user.\n   4. **Implement Independent Category Accordion System per Floor (Section 2A\342\200\2232E)**:\n      - Group works within the active floor (`Umum & Pondasi`, `Lantai 1`, `Lantai 2`, etc.) by USC category (`Persiapan Dll`, `Struktural`, `Arsitektural`, `MEP`).\n      - Add independent expand/collapse state keyed by `${floorId}::${category}` so opening `Arsitektural` never opens `Struktural` or `MEP`, and switching floors preserves each floor\'s category drawer states.\n      - Display `\342\226\266 Kategori (N pekerjaan)` / `\342\226\274 Kategori (N pekerjaan)` along with unfilled count (`X belum diisi`) and verified count.\n      - Add **Show All** (expands all categories on current floor) and **Minimalis** (collapses all categories on current floor) buttons in the floor toolbar.\n   5. **Optimize AI Quantity Takeoff Assistant (Section 3A\342\200\2233H)**:\n      - Expand classification to all 16 required drawing types (`Denah arsitektur`, `Denah struktur`, `Denah pondasi`, `Denah kolom`, `Denah balok`, `Denah sloof`, `Denah pembesian`, `Gambar potongan`, `Gambar tampak`, `Detail konstruksi`, `Detail penulangan`, `Tabel dimensi atau schedule`, `Gambar tangga`, `Gambar atap`, `Gambar MEP`, `Tidak diketahui / perlu pemeriksaan manual`).\n      - Ensure each extracted item & segment includes `pageNumber`, `drawingType`, `drawingTitle`, `floor`, `gridLocation`, `elementCode`, `rawExtractedValue`, `rawUnit`, `convertedValue`, `sourceInfo`, and `verificationBadge` (`Terbaca Jelas` | `Hasil Penggabungan` | `Perlu Verifikasi` | `Tidak Ditemukan`).\n      - Enhance beam (`B1`, `B2`, etc.) and sloof (`S1`, `S2`, etc.) segment calculation and UI breakdown display (`Segmen A\342\200\223B: 3,00 m`, etc. + `Total panjang`), preventing perimeter fallback and double-counting at intersections.\n      - Ensure structural table/schedule matching (`K1`, `B1`, `S1`) links cross-section and reinforcement data accurately by `elementCode` without cross-contaminating `B1` and `B2`.\n      - Add document/page hash caching (scoped to `userId + projectId`), step-by-step progress display, and clear error differentiation in `/server.ts` and the frontend AI modal/panel.\n   6. **Run Mandatory Verification (Section 5 & Section 6)**:\n      - Run automated verification scripts testing Account A vs Account B isolation, category accordion independence + Show All / Minimalis, and AI Quantity Takeoff multi-page classification, segment summation, and USC mapping.\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to ensure zero build/TypeScript errors, then provide the structured 6-point report in Indonesian.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Do not rebuild the app from scratch or remove any existing features listed in Section 4.\n   - Maintain Indonesian UI copy and civil engineering terminology (`Struktural`, `Arsitektural`, `MEP`, `Belum Diisi`, `Perlu Verifikasi`, `Terverifikasi`).\n   - All Gemini API calls must remain strictly server-side in `/server.ts`.\n</summary>"
