  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Login Data**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on `/src/services/projectStorage.ts`, specifically lines 1359-1442. My current hypothesis is that the `loadAllProjects(userId)` function (lines 1365-1442) is the key culprit behind users seeing data from prior sessions. I\'m focusing on the logic within this function to understand how user ID mismatches might be occurring during the data retrieval process.\n\n\n**Analyzing Legacy Data Loading**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause! The `loadAllProjects(userId)` function erroneously reads from `localStorage` under the `LEGACY_STORAGE_KEY_PROJECTS` key, specifically line 1359, which was used in the app\'s initial version. This key stores projects from the era before user accounts. This is why the legacy demo projects are still loading. The legacy projects are being loaded and, through some issue, displayed to the user.\n\n\n**Uncovering Persistent Data Injection**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the issue\'s persistence. The problematic code, particularly lines 1416-1422, injects legacy, unowned projects into every new or existing account, regardless of prior user data. Even if a user already has projects, this code checks if the legacy projects\' IDs already exist, and adds them if not. This ensures EVERY user, even after they log in to the system, sees the legacy projects from the `legacyUserProjects` array, because that data is being continually added to EVERY account.\n\n\n"
